\begin{definition}
\label{def:2-9-extra-1}



For smooth manifolds $M,N$, a diffeomorphism is a smooth bijection $F:M\to N$ whose inverse is smooth. The manifolds are diffeomorphic, written $M\approx N$, when such a map exists.
\end{definition}

